   9:     Slide multi-color sprites to align their marker pixels with matching isolated border anchors.
  10: 
  11:     Input structure:
  12:     - bg = most common color.
  13:     - Multi-color sprites in the interior; each has a minority-color "marker" pixel.
  14:     - Isolated border pixels (non-bg with all 4-neighbors bg) act as anchors.
  15: 
  16:     Rule:
  17:     - Match each sprite to the border anchor sharing its marker color.
  18:     - Top/bottom-edge anchor (non-corner): slide sprite horizontally so marker column = anchor column.
  19:     - Left/right-edge anchor (or corner): slide sprite vertically so marker row = anchor row.
  20: 
  21:     Key insight: The anchor's edge position determines the slide axis — top/bottom means horizontal, left/right (or corner) means vertical.
  22:     """
  23:     g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)
  24:     H, W = g.shape
  25:     bg = int(get_bg(g))
  26: 
  27:     def is_border(r: int, c: int) -> bool:
  28:         return int(r) in (0, int(H - 1)) or int(c) in (0, int(W - 1))
